"63_cocoaui_stub.mst — CG1 placeholder for the conditional Cocoa GUI world
 layer (docs/cocoa_gui_design.md §12.3, sprint_cocoa_gui.md CG1). Loaded ONLY
 via `frontend::world::load_list(vm, world/cocoaui.list)`, NEVER from
 world/world.list — so the CLI, the WKWebView GUI, and the base test suite
 carry none of it. Its whole job in CG1 is to prove the extra layer compiles
 and runs on top of an already-booted base world (a fresh class that is absent
 from the base world, present only after load_list). The real CocoaUI /
 view-wrapper classes arrive in CG2+ (files 64+)."
"I am a tiny marker class for the optional native-GUI world layer, which
 loads on top of an already-booted base world. I exist to prove that layer
 compiles and runs: `ping` answers a Symbol a headless check can verify.
 I have no other behavior."
Object subclass: CocoaUIStub [
    "A trivial marker from the conditional layer. `ping` answers a Symbol so a
     headless gate can prove not just that the class resolves but that a method
     of it actually runs (an oop from the extra layer, printString-checkable)."
    CocoaUIStub class >> ping [ ^#cocoaUiStubReady ]
]

"── STHostService — the MACDART host binding (ST_PLAN Sprint 14) ─────────
 MACVM's browsers talked to an ObjC MacvmHostService because their image
 data lived in the Rust host. OURS lives in the workspace language isolate
 — the very isolate the browser code runs in — so the host service is pure
 Smalltalk: each read is a direct <stprim:> into dart:cocoa, answered by
 the workspace's image hook (language.dart installs it over the SQLite
 decls). Replies are Smalltalk Strings in the exact wire formats the
 parsers expect (US-separated fields, space-separated token lists).
 onMain answers self: there is nothing to hop for. Image WRITES are
 read-only in v1 — edit through the workspace Browser; Accept here says
 so instead of failing silently."
Object subclass: STHostService [
    onMain [ ^self ]
    packageTree [ <stprim: stHostPackageTree> ]
    browseRecords [ <stprim: stHostBrowseRecords> ]
    commentFor: cls [ <stprim: stHostComment> ]
    classSourceFor: cls [ <stprim: stHostClassSource> ]
    sourceForClass: cls side: side selector: sel [ <stprim: stHostMethodSource> ]
    requestBrowser2Refresh [ CocoaBrowser2 doRefresh ]
    colorizeStorage: ts [ ^self ]
    saveMethodFor: cls side: side source: text [ <stprim: stHostSaveMethod> ]
    newClassFrom: text [ <stprim: stHostNewClass> ]
    setCommentFor: cls comment: text [ <stprim: stHostSetComment> ]
    acceptEditorClass: text [ <stprim: stHostAcceptClass> ]
    "Persist a class the PROGRAM generated (a saved table, a preferences
     holder), parse-checked and stored exactly like the accept above — but
     WITHOUT hot-reloading the world. The accept's reload re-inits every class's
     class-side state, which nils the frame loop's step block and freezes a
     running game on the frame that saved; this makes only the saved class live.
     Save from inside a running callback through here, not acceptEditorClass:."
    storeEditorClass: text [ <stprim: stHostStoreClass> ]
    removeClassNamed: cls [ <stprim: stHostRemoveClass> ]
    removeMethodFor: cls side: side selector: sel [ <stprim: stHostRemoveMethod> ]
]
